Some comments:&#x20;

- I thought we had started looking into not only complex p, but also q, because we were looking at \sqrt D. Perhaps you glossed over, but I think that is an important point if it is not central in the manuscript.&#x20;
- For your strongest preference, what do you mean by "estimating the final gap quantity"? I don't think I fully understand that.



This is out of left field, but your point about a common multiplicative normalization disappearing from H_z/H reminds me of localization work from Pestun that I worked on in grad school, for Wilson loops on a four sphere. The Atiyah Singer index theorem can be very powerful for these types of cancellations. We've discussed this angle before, but given the current results, I'm wondering if it could be relevant.
